# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Xiaoqing Liu et al. (2026). Fine-tuning universal machine-learned interatomic potentials: A Tutorial on methods and applications.
#   Journal of Applied Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0299305  arXiv:2506.21935v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2506.21935v2 (sha256 d02effddd0479579...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 231 (Overview/taxonomy). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the fine-tuned MACE models of the tutorial's examples
# with tabulated errors: LGPS fine-tuned from MACE-MP-0b3, MACE-MPA-0 and
# MACE-OMAT-0 (Table IV, after stochastic weight averaging), the
# LiCl(001)/GaF3(001) interface model fine-tuned from MACE-MPA-0
# (Table VIII), and the graphene-water model with its MD timings
# (Table VII). The Mo, silicon and Au2-MgO examples report properties or
# figures only; the review parts (Tables I-III) are not encoded.

