###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Fine-tuning and MD on a single NVIDIA A800 GPU (80 GB). MD wall-clock
# times for 10,000 steps (Table VII): 128 to 2,900 atoms, 710 to 2,619 s
# with cuEquivariance and 658 to 5,084 s without; the per-atom times for
# 2,900 atoms are held in the encoding input (no accuracy result for the
# graphene-water model is tabulated).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table IV gives each LGPS model before and after stochastic weight averaging; the final (after-SWA) values are encoded, the epoch-110 values are not. Relative force errors are not encoded.
# - The MACE-MP-0b3, MPA-0 and OMAT-0 checkpoints are named without size or release date, so they are not linked to registry models (base models are recorded as labels in the encoding input).
# - The silicon and Au2-MgO comparisons are figures (Figs. 5, 10); Mo results are elastic constants and stacking-fault barrier errors (Tables V, VI). Fine-tuning hyperparameters are discussed in Table III as recommendations, not per run.
# - Which foundation model was fine-tuned for the graphene-water interface is not stated explicitly; MACE-MPA-0 is the comparison model in Fig. 9.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

